    <Metadata Title="Happy Dungeons" Name="Decouple gameplay from frame rate (real time everywhere)" Author="local" Note="Every game timing follows real time at any frame rate: real delta time into the engine timer, the engine fps setting follows the measured frame rate (fixes ~100 seconds-to-frames conversions), the integer 1/60 s clock and the fps==60 special case count real time, and the rapid stab mash window is 467 ms at any fps. Online co-op is input lockstep, so there every player runs the same fixed 60 Hz tick (each step exactly 1/60 s; faster PCs pace their frames to it, slower ones such as 30 fps run several steps per frame) and players on any frame rate stay in sync. Built by tools\make_fps_patch.py. Caves at eboot 0x27af100 / 0x27af000, state at 0x5d36000." PatchVer="3.2" AppVer="01.11" AppElf="eboot.bin" isEnabled="true">
